%description:

Tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks:linux-ato -- after the quickack budget, a lone segment waits for the ATO, not for delayedAckTimeout.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "[...] an adaptive delay (ATO: from 40 ms, after the gaps between
arrivals, at most the SRTT and 200 ms) in place of delayedAckTimeout".

The classes: rfc (false), and three facets of true (LinuxTcp); this is the facet of the
adaptive delay. The code: each ACK uses one ACK of the quickack budget (ackSent()); when the
budget is gone, a lone segment schedules the delayed ACK after the ATO, which starts at 40 ms
(scheduleDelayedAck()). A pause shorter than the RTO gives no new budget. This test
separates the facet from "rfc": with false, the lone segment waits 200 ms.

Host under test: host2, the receiver. Peer: host1 sends 30000 bytes at 0.2 s, which use up
the quickack budget, and one segment of 100 bytes at 0.8 s. Observation: level 1, the ACK of
host2 for the lone segment: none in the first 30 ms after its arrival, one in the next 70 ms.

%# parameter: Tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks
%# class: linux-ato
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxAto")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the SYN of host1")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 30001 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the lone segment of 100 bytes at host2")
                  .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                   .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                   .describe("an ACK of host2 in the first 30 ms")
                   .within(0.03))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .describe("the delayed ACK of host2, after the ATO")
                  .within(0.07));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxAto compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 0B
*.host1.app[0].sendScript = "0.2 30000; 0.8 100"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxAto: PASS
